note left of WebAdapter
**Web Adapter Commands:**
```python
# Playwright execution example
async def execute_web_action(command):
    if command.action == "click":
        element = await page.wait_for_selector(command.target)
        await element.click()

        # Verify success
        success_indicator = command.validation
        if success_indicator:
            await page.wait_for_selector(success_indicator)

        # Capture result state
        screenshot = await page.screenshot()
        return ExecutionResult(
            success=True,
            screenshot_after=base64.encode(screenshot),
            metadata={"url": page.url, "title": await page.title()}
        )
```

**Command Translation:**
• GPT Output → Playwright commands
• Error handling & retries
• State verification
• Performance tracking
end note

note left of DesktopAdapter
**Desktop Adapter Commands:**
```python
# Desktop execution example
async def execute_desktop_action(command):
    if command.action == "click":
        x, y = parse_coordinates(command.target)

        # Windows API click
        if platform == "windows":
            import pyautogui
            pyautogui.click(x, y)

        # Verify by screenshot comparison
        after_screenshot = capture_screenshot()
        success = verify_state_change(after_screenshot)

        return ExecutionResult(
            success=success,
            screenshot_after=base64.encode(after_screenshot)
        )
```

**Coordinate Translation:**
• GPT-4V relative coords → absolute pixels
• Multi-monitor support
• Window focus management
end note

note left of MobileAdapter
**Mobile Adapter Commands:**
```python
# Appium execution example
async def execute_mobile_action(command):
    if command.action == "tap":
        if "coordinates" in command.parameters:
            x, y = command.parameters["coordinates"]
            driver.tap([(x, y)])
        else:
            element = driver.find_element(AppiumBy.ID, command.target)
            element.click()

        # Wait for UI to update
        time.sleep(0.5)

        # Capture result
        screenshot = driver.get_screenshot_as_png()
        return ExecutionResult(
            success=True,
            screenshot_after=base64.encode(screenshot),
            metadata={"activity": driver.current_activity}
        )
```

**Platform Specifics:**
• Android: UIAutomator2 + ADB
• iOS: XCUITest + WebDriverAgent
• Touch gesture translation
end note

